      "problem": "$({x}^{m}-2{y}^{n})({x}^{m}+2{y}^{n})=$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)(a-b)={a}^{2}-{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a={x}^{m}$ and $b=2{y}^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{m}-2{y}^{n})({x}^{m}+2{y}^{n}) & = \\\\ {({x}^{m})}^{2}-{(2{y}^{n})}^{2} & = \\\\ {({x}^{m})}^{2}-{2}^{2}\\cdot {({y}^{n})}^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{2m}-4{y}^{2n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
